# What a run of the tooling leaves behind, and none of which belongs in the history.
#
# The two reports under `ci/report/` and `validation/report/` are **not** here: those are committed
# artefacts, refreshed by the commit hook and staged with the change that moved them, so that a
# reader of this repository on the web sees the figures without running anything.

__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.benchmarks/

# The measurements the CI commands write, which `ci-check` then judges. Facts about one commit on
# one machine: `make ci-fast` writes them again in seconds, and carrying them in the history would
# put a diff in every commit saying where somebody's laptop got to.
/reports/

# The structured log, which a run at `-vvv` writes into the directory it was started from rather
# than into its output directory. Ignored so that turning the verbosity up is not also a dirty
# branch.
freeports.log.jsonl
